{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"736489857928396840","content":"\"FLAMENCO?\" He pulls a flower out of his flower crown and puts it between his teeth. Or perhaps a courtly waltz?\" He picks a broom and spins about rhythmically.","created_at":"2020-07-28T23:10:35.201000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-28T23:11:00.912000Z","id":"737809259093557339","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"736489857928396840","content":"She laughs, \"I'll read anything you give me. But...\" She thinks for a moment, \"Do you have a book with all kinds of dancing in it? I don't need anything detailed, I just want to see what there is. Dancing has always seemed strange to me. In a Goblin tribe you only ever dance for specific things, and I never really considered those things happy.\" She looks a bit sad but doesn't dwell on it long. \"But when I came to London, in the Fat Friar, you sang and danced so proudly and I could tell it made you happy. But I don't want to dance just to fit in, I want to do it to make it my own.\" She beams up at him, jaggedy teeth and all.","created_at":"2020-07-28T23:25:29.739000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-28T23:27:00.535000Z","id":"737813011057868911","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
